            <ArticleTitle>Stent implantation to the stenosed right coronary artery in a patient whose right and left coronary arteries originate from a single ostium in the right sinus of Valsalva.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>101-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a rare case of a patient who had anomalous origin of left and right coronary arteries from a single coronary ostium in the right sinus of Valsalva. The stenosed right coronary artery was successfully dilated with stent implantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
